Nix64 patch 0004: warp, the RESTORE key, and an instant flush for the Stop key

Applies on top of patches 0001 to 0003. Version 4 of the shared-memory file (size unchanged).

Two new input events in the ring (patch 0002):
  type 4 RESTORE  a = 1 down / 0 up. The RESTORE key is not in the keyboard matrix (it pulls NMI),
                  so it cannot be a type 1 key event. Calls machine_set_restore_key().
  type 5 WARP     a = 1 warp on / 0 warp off. Calls vsync_set_warp_mode(). VICE has no resource for
                  warp (setting Speed to 0 is refused), so this is the only way to toggle it at runtime
                  without a window or a hotkey.
And one control word: header word reserved[0] (offset 24). The client increments it to say "drop
everything queued, let go of every key and stick": the ring head jumps to the tail, the keyboard
matrix, the keyboard buffer, both joystick ports and RESTORE are cleared. This is the Stop key for
whoever is driving the machine (the Nix64 agent): it works at once, however much typing is still queued.
Older readers keep working. Against: VICE 3.10 with patches 0001 to 0003. License: GPL-2.0-or-later.

